    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d848">

                <pb facs="0822" n="810" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg810"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/1950</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Secretary of War</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stimson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-09-01">September 1, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I refer to my
                    conversations with you early in August regarding a proposal for the issuance of
                    a joint statement by the American and British Governments regarding
                    Palestine.</p>
                <p>As the result of the opinion which you expressed to me on August 5 that the
                    situation in Palestine is not serious enough from a military point of view to
                    warrant the issuance of a statement along these lines, we informed the British
                    Government that in view of this opinion of the War Department no basis exists,
                    so far as the United States is concerned, for issuing the statement, in as much
                    as its sole purpose was to ameliorate a condition which was thought to be
                    dangerous in the <pb facs="0823" n="811" xml:id="pg811"/> military sense. The
                    British Foreign Minister and Minister for the Colonies stated that they were
                    greatly disappointed at this decision.</p>
                <p>At Quebec, on August 21, the British handed to us a communication concerning the
                    present situation and outlook with respect to Palestine, a copy of which is
                    enclosed herewith.<anchor n="99" xml:id="d848-f1"/> I should be grateful if,
                    after reading the British communication, you would let me have your views
                    regarding it.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cordell Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
